          "headline": "Journalist Frenchie Mae Cumpio Convicted of Terror Financing - Up to 18 Years",
          "headlineHref": "/interactive-timeline/index.html?date=2026-01-22&search=Journalist%20Frenchie%20Mae%20Cumpio%20Convicted%20of%20Terror%20Financing%20-%20Up%20to%2018%20Years",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>Tacloban RTC Branch 45 convicted journalist Frenchie Mae Cumpio, 26, and lay worker Marielle Domequil, 28, of terrorism financing and acquitted them of firearms and explosives charges. Both have been detained since February 2020. CPJ and RSF called the verdict a failure of press-freedom pledges; the defense said it would seek bail pending appeal.</p>",
