          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The Singapore-flagged MV Devon Bay, crewed by 21 Filipinos and carrying iron ore, capsized about 55 nautical miles from Scarborough Shoal. Two sailors died, four were missing, and 15 were rescued after Chinese coast-guard ships reached the scene first and the Philippine Coast Guard launched vessels and aircraft. Singapore's Maritime and Port Authority opened an investigation in disputed waters.</p>",
