          "headline": "AMRO Projects 5.3% GDP Growth for Philippines in 2026",
          "headlineHref": "/interactive-timeline/index.html?date=2026-01-22&search=AMRO%20Projects%205.3%25%20GDP%20Growth%20for%20Philippines%20in%202026",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The ASEAN+3 Macroeconomic Research Office projected 5.3 percent Philippine growth in 2026, second in Southeast Asia after Vietnam, even after Manila cut its official target to 5–6 percent following the flood-control scandal. Capital Economics was more cautious at 4.5 percent. Inflation was seen at 3.2 percent, with a 25-basis-point BSP cut still expected in the first quarter.</p>",
